{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.H3FrobeniusCasimirMarkovTrace","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.H3FrobeniusCasimirMarkovTrace","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Fin","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Rat.Defs"],"declarations":45,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassCore.H3FrobeniusCasimir.cdimq_tautology","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassCore.H3FrobeniusCasimir.cdimq_tautology","kind":"theorem","line":306,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/h3-frobenius-casimir-markov-trace.lean#L306-L314","doc":"The tautology behind the repo's `C_{dim_q}`: whatever the nonzero block\ntraces `t_λ`, the central element `Σ_λ e_λ / (dim_q λ · t_λ)` has trace\n`Σ_λ 1/dim_q λ`.  No property of the Frobenius structure is used. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassCore.H3FrobeniusCasimir.inv_qdim_sum_three_D","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassCore.H3FrobeniusCasimir.inv_qdim_sum_three_D","kind":"theorem","line":300,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/h3-frobenius-casimir-markov-trace.lean#L300-L304","doc":"Under convention D only `(3)` and `(2,1)` survive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassCore.H3FrobeniusCasimir.inv_qdim_sum_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassCore.H3FrobeniusCasimir.inv_qdim_sum_three","kind":"theorem","line":295,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/h3-frobenius-casimir-markov-trace.lean#L295-L298","doc":"`Σ_{λ ⊢ 3} 1/dim_q λ` with q-hook dimensions `dim_q(3) = dim_q(1,1,1) = 1`,\n`dim_q(2,1) = [2]_q = q + q⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassCore.H3FrobeniusCasimir.inv_qdim_eq_schur_sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassCore.H3FrobeniusCasimir.inv_qdim_eq_schur_sum","kind":"theorem","line":281,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/h3-frobenius-casimir-markov-trace.lean#L281-L291","doc":"The honest Frobenius reading of `Σ_{λ ⊢ 3} 1/dim_q λ`: it is\n`Σ_λ q^{-κ(λ)} c_λ / [3]_q!`, the sum of the bar-symmetrised Schur elements of\nthe canonical form divided by `[3]_q! = [2]_q [3]_q`; equivalently\n`dim_q λ = [3]_q! / (q^{-κ(λ)} c_λ)` is the balanced generic degree.  Stated with\n`[2]_q = (q²+1)/q`, `[3]_q = d3/q²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassCore.H3FrobeniusCasimir.tau0_schur","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassCore.H3FrobeniusCasimir.tau0_schur","kind":"theorem","line":271,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/h3-frobenius-casimir-markov-trace.lean#L271-L279","doc":"Schur elements of `τ₀`: `τ₀ = Σ_λ χ_λ / c_λ` with\n`c_(3) = (q²+1)d3 = q³[3]_q!`, `c_(2,1) = d3/q² = [3]_q`, `c_(1,1,1) = (q²+1)d3/q⁶ = q⁻³[3]_q!`,\ni.e. `c_λ = q^{κ(λ)} ∏_{hooks} [h]_q` (`κ` = content sum). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassCore.H3FrobeniusCasimir.tau0val","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassCore.H3FrobeniusCasimir.tau0val","kind":"def","line":268,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/h3-frobenius-casimir-markov-trace.lean#L268-L269","doc":"`τ₀(T_w) = δ_{w,1}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassCore.H3FrobeniusCasimir.tr_casimir_blocks","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassCore.H3FrobeniusCasimir.tr_casimir_blocks","kind":"theorem","line":247,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/h3-frobenius-casimir-markov-trace.lean#L247-L264","doc":"Consistency: `tr^z(C₀) = Σ_λ c_λ d_λ · d_λ y_λ(z)` with Schur elements\n`c_(3) = (q²+1)d3`, `c_(2,1) = d3/q²`, `c_(1,1,1) = (q²+1)d3/q⁶` (so `C₀` acts on\nthe block `λ` by `c_λ d_λ`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassCore.H3FrobeniusCasimir.yRefl_D","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassCore.H3FrobeniusCasimir.yRefl_D","kind":"theorem","line":236,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/h3-frobenius-casimir-markov-trace.lean#L236-L245","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassCore.H3FrobeniusCasimir.yTriv_D","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassCore.H3FrobeniusCasimir.yTriv_D","kind":"theorem","line":225,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/h3-frobenius-casimir-markov-trace.lean#L225-L234","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassCore.H3FrobeniusCasimir.ySign_D","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassCore.H3FrobeniusCasimir.ySign_D","kind":"theorem","line":219,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/h3-frobenius-casimir-markov-trace.lean#L219-L223","doc":"Convention D kills the sign block: `y_(1,1,1)(z_D) = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassCore.H3FrobeniusCasimir.markov_weights","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassCore.H3FrobeniusCasimir.markov_weights","kind":"theorem","line":204,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/h3-frobenius-casimir-markov-trace.lean#L204-L217","doc":"`tr^z = y_(3) χ_(3) + y_(2,1) χ_(2,1) + y_(1,1,1) χ_(1,1,1)` on every basis element. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassCore.H3FrobeniusCasimir.ySign","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassCore.H3FrobeniusCasimir.ySign","kind":"def","line":202,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/h3-frobenius-casimir-markov-trace.lean#L202-L202","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassCore.H3FrobeniusCasimir.yRefl","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassCore.H3FrobeniusCasimir.yRefl","kind":"def","line":201,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/h3-frobenius-casimir-markov-trace.lean#L201-L201","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassCore.H3FrobeniusCasimir.yTriv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassCore.H3FrobeniusCasimir.yTriv","kind":"def","line":200,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/h3-frobenius-casimir-markov-trace.lean#L200-L200","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassCore.H3FrobeniusCasimir.d3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassCore.H3FrobeniusCasimir.d3","kind":"def","line":197,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/h3-frobenius-casimir-markov-trace.lean#L197-L198","doc":"`[3]_q`-type denominator `(q²+q+1)(q²-q+1) = q⁴+q²+1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassCore.H3FrobeniusCasimir.chiRefl","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassCore.H3FrobeniusCasimir.chiRefl","kind":"def","line":195,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/h3-frobenius-casimir-markov-trace.lean#L195-L195","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassCore.H3FrobeniusCasimir.chiSign","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassCore.H3FrobeniusCasimir.chiSign","kind":"def","line":194,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/h3-frobenius-casimir-markov-trace.lean#L194-L194","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassCore.H3FrobeniusCasimir.chiTriv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassCore.H3FrobeniusCasimir.chiTriv","kind":"def","line":192,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/h3-frobenius-casimir-markov-trace.lean#L192-L193","doc":"characters of the three irreducibles on the basis `T_w`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassCore.H3FrobeniusCasimir.tr_casimir_D_ne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassCore.H3FrobeniusCasimir.tr_casimir_D_ne","kind":"theorem","line":186,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/h3-frobenius-casimir-markov-trace.lean#L186-L188","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassCore.H3FrobeniusCasimir.tr_casimir_q1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassCore.H3FrobeniusCasimir.tr_casimir_q1","kind":"theorem","line":180,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/h3-frobenius-casimir-markov-trace.lean#L180-L184","doc":"The identity `tr_M(C_Frob) = 2 + 1/[2]_q` fails for the Frobenius Casimir:\nat `q = 1` over `ℚ` the trace is `6` for every `z` (group algebra `ℚ[S₃]`,\nwhere `C₀ = 6·1`), while `2 + 1/[2]_1 = 5/2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassCore.H3FrobeniusCasimir.tr_casimir_D_sub","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassCore.H3FrobeniusCasimir.tr_casimir_D_sub","kind":"theorem","line":167,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/h3-frobenius-casimir-markov-trace.lean#L167-L178","doc":"Difference from the claimed value `2 + 1/[2]_q`, as a rational function. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassCore.H3FrobeniusCasimir.tr_casimir_D","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassCore.H3FrobeniusCasimir.tr_casimir_D","kind":"theorem","line":159,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/h3-frobenius-casimir-markov-trace.lean#L159-L165","doc":"**Markov trace of the Frobenius Casimir, convention D.** ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:h3-frobenius-casimir-markov-trace","label":"prop:h3-frobenius-casimir-markov-trace","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/h3-frobenius-casimir-markov-trace.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassCore.H3FrobeniusCasimir.tr_casimir","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassCore.H3FrobeniusCasimir.tr_casimir","kind":"theorem","line":149,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/h3-frobenius-casimir-markov-trace.lean#L149-L157","doc":"**Markov trace of the Frobenius Casimir, generic `z`.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassCore.H3FrobeniusCasimir.casimir_central","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassCore.H3FrobeniusCasimir.casimir_central","kind":"theorem","line":142,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/h3-frobenius-casimir-markov-trace.lean#L142-L147","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassCore.H3FrobeniusCasimir.casimir_coords","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassCore.H3FrobeniusCasimir.casimir_coords","kind":"theorem","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/h3-frobenius-casimir-markov-trace.lean#L137-L140","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassCore.H3FrobeniusCasimir.C0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassCore.H3FrobeniusCasimir.C0","kind":"def","line":134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/h3-frobenius-casimir-markov-trace.lean#L134-L135","doc":"`C₀ = Σ_w T_w T_{w⁻¹}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassCore.H3FrobeniusCasimir.tau0_dual","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassCore.H3FrobeniusCasimir.tau0_dual","kind":"theorem","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/h3-frobenius-casimir-markov-trace.lean#L123-L130","doc":"`T_{w⁻¹}` is the `τ₀`-dual basis: `τ₀(T_v T_{w⁻¹}) = δ_{v,w}`\n(`τ₀` = coefficient of `T_1`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassCore.H3FrobeniusCasimir.tr_markov","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassCore.H3FrobeniusCasimir.tr_markov","kind":"theorem","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/h3-frobenius-casimir-markov-trace.lean#L118-L121","doc":"Markov property: `tr(x σ₂) = z tr(x)` for `x ∈ H_2 = span{1, σ₁}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassCore.H3FrobeniusCasimir.tr_comm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassCore.H3FrobeniusCasimir.tr_comm","kind":"theorem","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/h3-frobenius-casimir-markov-trace.lean#L111-L116","doc":"`tr^z` is a trace on basis elements: `tr(T_v T_w) = tr(T_w T_v)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassCore.H3FrobeniusCasimir.mul_b","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassCore.H3FrobeniusCasimir.mul_b","kind":"theorem","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/h3-frobenius-casimir-markov-trace.lean#L104-L109","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassCore.H3FrobeniusCasimir.LT_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassCore.H3FrobeniusCasimir.LT_one","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/h3-frobenius-casimir-markov-trace.lean#L98-L100","doc":"the basis vectors multiply as expected: `T_w · 1 = T_w` (sanity check). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassCore.H3FrobeniusCasimir.braid","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassCore.H3FrobeniusCasimir.braid","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/h3-frobenius-casimir-markov-trace.lean#L94-L96","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassCore.H3FrobeniusCasimir.sigma2_quad","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassCore.H3FrobeniusCasimir.sigma2_quad","kind":"theorem","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/h3-frobenius-casimir-markov-trace.lean#L90-L92","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassCore.H3FrobeniusCasimir.sigma1_quad","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassCore.H3FrobeniusCasimir.sigma1_quad","kind":"theorem","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/h3-frobenius-casimir-markov-trace.lean#L86-L88","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassCore.H3FrobeniusCasimir.zD","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassCore.H3FrobeniusCasimir.zD","kind":"def","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/h3-frobenius-casimir-markov-trace.lean#L81-L82","doc":"convention D. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassCore.H3FrobeniusCasimir.tr","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassCore.H3FrobeniusCasimir.tr","kind":"def","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/h3-frobenius-casimir-markov-trace.lean#L78-L79","doc":"the Ocneanu/Markov trace with parameter `z`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassCore.H3FrobeniusCasimir.tval","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassCore.H3FrobeniusCasimir.tval","kind":"def","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/h3-frobenius-casimir-markov-trace.lean#L75-L76","doc":"values `tr^z(T_w)` of the Ocneanu trace. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassCore.H3FrobeniusCasimir.invIdx","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassCore.H3FrobeniusCasimir.invIdx","kind":"def","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/h3-frobenius-casimir-markov-trace.lean#L71-L73","doc":"index of `w⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassCore.H3FrobeniusCasimir.mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassCore.H3FrobeniusCasimir.mul","kind":"def","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/h3-frobenius-casimir-markov-trace.lean#L68-L69","doc":"the algebra product `x * y = Σ_w x_w T_w y`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassCore.H3FrobeniusCasimir.b","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassCore.H3FrobeniusCasimir.b","kind":"def","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/h3-frobenius-casimir-markov-trace.lean#L65-L66","doc":"basis vector. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassCore.H3FrobeniusCasimir.LT","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassCore.H3FrobeniusCasimir.LT","kind":"def","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/h3-frobenius-casimir-markov-trace.lean#L56-L63","doc":"left multiplication by the basis element `T_w`, `w` indexed by `Fin 6`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassCore.H3FrobeniusCasimir.L2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassCore.H3FrobeniusCasimir.L2","kind":"def","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/h3-frobenius-casimir-markov-trace.lean#L52-L54","doc":"left multiplication by `σ₂`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassCore.H3FrobeniusCasimir.L1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassCore.H3FrobeniusCasimir.L1","kind":"def","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/h3-frobenius-casimir-markov-trace.lean#L48-L50","doc":"left multiplication by `σ₁`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassCore.H3FrobeniusCasimir.hh","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassCore.H3FrobeniusCasimir.hh","kind":"def","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/h3-frobenius-casimir-markov-trace.lean#L45-L46","doc":"`h = q - q⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassCore.H3FrobeniusCasimir.V","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassCore.H3FrobeniusCasimir.V","kind":"def","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/h3-frobenius-casimir-markov-trace.lean#L41-L43","doc":"coordinates of an element of `H_3(q)` in the basis\n`[1, σ₁, σ₂, σ₁σ₂, σ₂σ₁, σ₁σ₂σ₁]`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}